# Authoring editors, driven from the front end: Title -> main menu -> "Play now" ->
# the world splash -> Choose Your World -> "... or Create Your Own World ..." (front state 9/10)
# -> the Link Editor. Place a link, place a monster, paint one terrain cell, save, leave.
#
# This replay MUTATES the world binaries, so it must be run against a copy of extracted/;
# tests/editors_replay.sh does that and byte-diffs the result.
# requires: editor_open editor_link_add editor_monster editor_terrain editor_save editor_screen
# The title screen turns any key into the main menu, so no boot_menu expect is needed.
key RETURN
wait 20
# FUN_00402A73's Terms of Service modal opens on entry to the main menu (front.c:534
# tos_gate, consumed at front.c:770) and swallows the next key. "I Accept" is
# tos_accept = (356,371,75,23), so its centre is (393,382).
click 393 382
expect tos_accept 300
key RETURN
wait 20
key x
wait 60
# "--- or Create Your Own World ---" is FUN_0041D3CC's 1000x1000-space rect (1000,1000)-
# (875,875); after its 750 ms slide it lands at (560,420) with the text's width, so the
# on-screen part is x 560..640, y 420..428.
click 600 424
# editor_open is logged by editors_load_map before editors_enter() screen_sets, so it must be
# expected first: an `expect` that matches advances the replay's baseline past that event.
expect editor_open 300
expect editor_screen 300
# 1 = link tool: click to put the cursor on the map, then N to claim the lowest free .obl
# record at the cursor (the editor's "Add" entry). Every shipped sprite covers almost the whole
# map, so the click selects an existing link and N is what actually places one.
key 1
wait 2
click 700 30
expect editor_link_select 120
key n
expect editor_link_add 120
# 3 = monster tool: a click places into the lowest free .mon record. (60,60) is cell
# (15,15), 67 cells from the nearest shipped monster.
key 3
wait 2
click 60 60
expect editor_monster 120
# 2 = terrain tool: a click paints the brush square, the right button erases it.
key 2
wait 2
click 200 200
expect editor_terrain 120
# Leaving with unsaved links raises FUN_0045C7D7's MessageBox: "Save your link changes for map
# %s?" / "Hmmm.." with MB_YESNO, drawn in framebuffer at (200,258) Yes / (340,258) No.
# The `dialog` op can answer it as `dialog 61441 ok` (EDITOR_DIALOG_SAVE_LINKS) once Core routes
# the op to editors_dialog_op; Y / N / Enter / Esc and the two buttons work today.
key ESCAPE
expect editor_prompt 120
key y
expect editor_save 300
expect editor_leave 300
quit
